{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And over his host, Nachshon son of Amminadav</b> – I do not know why Scripture mentions here the names of the princes of the standards, since it has already mentioned this. And if you say to hint that they were alive, this was already hinted at in the pericope of the standards (Numbers 2:4), for from the day of the census until the time of the journey not one of all those counted had died. Perhaps Scripture comes to say that even when they travel on the road, the prince goes at the head of his host, so that they should fulfill his command and he should dwell like a king in the camp, and they should not travel like sheep that have no shepherd, nor should they appoint another over them for this, as is done with an anointed one for battle."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:03:58.905806478Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}